---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Software for school and nonprofit ceramics programs"
	description="Kilnbook runs class registration, waitlists, firing queues and wheel time for nonprofit ceramics programs and school studios, with 30% off any plan."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Schools &amp; nonprofits</p>
				<h1>Studio software at a nonprofit price.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Class registration, waitlists, firing queues and wheel time in one place, built for pottery
					studios. Registered nonprofits and school ceramics programs get 30% off any plan.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/class-pack.svg"
				alt="A six-class pack card with three classes used and a waitlist card for a Tuesday evening session"
				width="480"
				height="320"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
			<h2>Running a program on a small budget</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"Is there still a spot?"</h3>
					<p>
						Classes fill fast, and every cancellation means working down a waitlist by email or phone.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"Whose pot is this?"</h3>
					<p>
						Dozens of students share the same kilns, and unlabelled work piles up on the pickup shelf.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"We can't pay gym prices."</h3>
					<p>
						Most booking software is priced for commercial studios, and a ceramics program's budget
						goes on clay and kiln repairs first.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>For programs that teach clay</h2>
		<p>
			Community art centres, nonprofit ceramics programs and school studios run on classes and
			shared kilns, often with a small staff and volunteers. Kilnbook handles the bookings and the
			firing log so the people you have can teach.
		</p>

		<h2>Registration and waitlists that run themselves</h2>
		<p>
			Set up courses and drop-in sessions once and let students book and pay online. When a class is
			full, students join the waitlist, and a cancelled seat is offered to the next person by text
			without anyone on staff stepping in. <a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Instructors see their roster</h2>
		<p>
			Instructors get their own login with today's roster, who has paid and who is new to clay. They
			can mark attendance from the studio tablet and leave notes for the next instructor.
		</p>

		<h2>Every piece tracked through the kiln</h2>
		<p>
			Students log a piece when they put it on the bisque shelf. Kilnbook puts it in the right load,
			charges a firing fee if you set one, and texts them when it is ready to collect.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>30% off any plan</h2>
		<p>
			Registered nonprofits and school ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention it when you
			book a demo. You can bring your existing student list over from a spreadsheet during setup.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="band-dark quote-band">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<blockquote class="quote">
				We used to spend Sunday nights reconciling the kiln log with Venmo. Now the log is the
				invoice.
				<cite>Dana Whitlock, owner, Mudroom Ceramics (Tacoma, WA)</cite>
			</blockquote>
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Proof</p>
				<h2>Built by people who load kilns</h2>
				<p>
					Kilnbook is a nine-person team, and several of us throw every week. Over 340 studios in the
					US, Canada and the UK run their bookings, firings and memberships on it.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Spend less time on the sign-up sheet.</h2>
			<p>30 days free to start. No card needed. Ask about nonprofit pricing when you book.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
